{"duration_api_ms":217249,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"fc1e429f-f63b-4743-aa85-e055a3db83e7","total_cost_usd":0.265712,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13267,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":21264,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":15368},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13267,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":21264,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13267,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13267},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":21264,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":13267,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.265712,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":15368,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The feasible front is a single narrow curve of large, blunt, flat capsules (d 3.2-3.3 m, bluntness 1.05-1.2, cone 68-69.5 deg) swept over flight-path angle. Bondline temperature dominates the hypervolume, because its normalised gap to the reference is large while peak flux is already about 0.1 of its reference. Temperature falls with steeper entry, but max_g <= 12 caps steepness near -3.6 deg. The heatshield mass fraction caps diameter near 3.38 m at bluntness 1.2. The 9 geometry failures all come from a cone angle too small for the bluntness, and no failure sits at the high-bluntness, high-cone corner I propose.\",\"evidence\":[\"Front at d 3.2, b 1.05, cone 68 (C-64136d63e115, C-963dbfd623f8, C-f05827094e99, C-ad32f7fbb36b, C-06797c928cfb, C-935f6de2005a): FPA -1.6 to -3.6 gives T 425.0 to 397.6 K and q 272k to 326k W/m2, so steeper entry trades q for T. It flattens near -3.5 to -3.6.\",\"g depends mainly on FPA and weakly on d: g = 11.93 at (d 3.2, -3.6) in C-935f6de2005a, 11.85 at (d 3.0, -3.6) in C-6273db35a5a3, and 11.52 at (d 3.4, -3.3) in C-bd7e4639d608. That puts the g=12 limit at about -3.6 to -3.65 deg.\",\"Larger d and larger b lower both q and T: C-bd7e4639d608 (d 3.4, b 1.2, -3.3) has q 283k and T 396.1, versus C-891309de2478 (d 3.3, b 1.05, -3.3) with q 303k and T 398.9. C-bd7e4639d608 fails only on mass fraction (-0.0089), while C-991bedc32808 (d 3.3) has +0.0496. So the d limit is about 3.38 at b 1.2.\",\"Mass fraction margin is 0.1063 for C-b392d085ef3b (b 1.2, cone 69.5) against 0.1007 for C-935f6de2005a (b 1.05, cone 68) at d 3.2. Higher b and cone angle therefore help slightly.\",\"Geometry failures: C-f5b5877d7e46 (b 0.79, cone 52) and C-d908ebc2f4b2 (b 0.87, cone 56.7). Feasible geometries: C-b392d085ef3b (b 1.2, cone 69.5) and C-5bb643430fbf (b 0.85, cone 66). The minimum cone angle rises with bluntness, so b > 1.2 may need a cone above 70 deg. The b 1.3-1.35 probes carry real risk.\",\"Small-d designs (C-e9e313e4732c, d 2.2: q 546k, T 426) are dominated by the large-d front, so I am not exploring there.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak flux scales roughly as 1/sqrt(nose radius), and nose radius is proportional to b*d. Bondline temperature falls with a larger d (lower ballistic coefficient, lower heat load) and with a steeper, shorter entry pulse, until max_g binds. I fitted local scalings from the data: q falls about 4% per +0.1 m of d and about 3% per +0.15 of b; T falls about 2.3 K per +0.1 m of d, with b having little effect. The plan is to push d to about 3.36 m (mass fraction margin about 0.015) at b 1.2 and cone 69.5, sweep FPA from -1.5 to -3.6 to fill the front, and probe higher b/cone for a further flux reduction. I am relying partly on these local fits and partly on prior knowledge of entry heating scaling.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The mass-fraction margin near d 3.36-3.38 is a linear extrapolation and could go negative. The g margin at FPA -3.6 with d 3.36 is only about 0.002 by my estimate. The geometry threshold for b > 1.2 is unknown and those proposals may return no metrics. The d, b and FPA scalings come from sparse points and may be nonlinear.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-b392d085ef3b\",\"rationale\":\"Steepest-entry corner of the front at a larger d: minimum T just under the g limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":296000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether g stays below 12 at d 3.36 and -3.6, and gives the lowest T on the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b392d085ef3b\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly less steep, safer on g, still low T.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":293400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks the d 3.36 mass-fraction margin and the larger-d benefit in a safe region.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b392d085ef3b\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-steep point at larger d, replacing the d 3.3 b 1.05 point with lower q and T.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":287000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Anchors the new front near the previous bd7e point, which was infeasible only on mass fraction.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b392d085ef3b\",\"rationale\":\"Fills the middle of the front at d 3.36.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":280600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves coverage of the trade-off curve.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b392d085ef3b\",\"rationale\":\"Front coverage between -3.0 and -2.5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.75},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":403.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a front gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b392d085ef3b\",\"rationale\":\"Low-flux side of the front at larger d.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":268000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":406.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Should dominate C-991bedc32808 (d 3.3, -2.5: q 274.8k, T 407.6) on both objectives.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b392d085ef3b\",\"rationale\":\"Front coverage in the flux-favoured region.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":262000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a front gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b392d085ef3b\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow entry, low flux.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":256000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":413.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Should extend the front to lower flux than 281.6k at T 418.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b392d085ef3b\",\"rationale\":\"Between -2.0 and -1.6, densifying the low-flux end.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":251000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":417.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a front gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b392d085ef3b\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow end of the front at larger d.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":247000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":420.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Should dominate C-64136d63e115 (q 271.9k, T 425).\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b392d085ef3b\",\"rationale\":\"Shallowest allowed FPA, minimum-flux extreme.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":244000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":422.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the front at the low-q extreme; T is still below 450 there.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b392d085ef3b\",\"rationale\":\"Maximum bluntness and cone angle should cut q about 3% and may improve mass fraction.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":278400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the geometry boundary at the corner of the design space and the benefit of higher b.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b392d085ef3b\",\"rationale\":\"Intermediate b 1.3 with the maximum cone angle; a smaller geometry risk than b 1.35.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.3,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":287500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes whether b 1.3 at cone 70 is buildable and whether it lowers q.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b392d085ef3b\",\"rationale\":\"Isolates the effect of cone 70 versus 69.5 at b 1.2.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":293000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Measures the cone-angle effect on mass fraction, q and T.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-bd7e4639d608\",\"rationale\":\"Push d toward the mass-fraction limit (about 3.385 by linear extrapolation).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":291000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the mass-fraction boundary between d 3.36 and 3.4.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b392d085ef3b\",\"rationale\":\"Higher-b, shallow-side probe at cone 70.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.3,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":262600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":406.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether higher b gives a lower-flux front in the mid range, if the geometry is valid.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b392d085ef3b\",\"rationale\":\"Higher-b, mid-range probe.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.3,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":275000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Second point on the b 1.3 line, so the b effect can be separated from FPA.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b392d085ef3b\",\"rationale\":\"Maximum bluntness at shallow entry to minimise q.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.35,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":248000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":413.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the flux floor at maximum b if the geometry is valid.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b392d085ef3b\",\"rationale\":\"Smaller d, steep entry, moderately higher b and cone 70, for a different tradeoff and geometry point.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":300000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Larger mass-fraction margin than d 3.36 near the g limit, and a test of b 1.25 at cone 70.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b392d085ef3b\",\"rationale\":\"Fill between -3.5 and -3.6 at d 3.36.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":294600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the g-limit edge of the front while staying probably feasible.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":171983,"type":"result","duration_ms":217282,"uuid":"8164906e-5dd6-4e5d-b90c-93e13a74f989","ttft_stream_ms":998,"time_to_request_ms":31,"first_content_frame_ms":998,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
